From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 04:58:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] feat(appointments): enforce approved V1 lifecycle rules
 (PM-APPT-01..05)

- PM-APPT-01: a patient may cancel or reschedule only while now < start_at.
- PM-APPT-02: nobody may cancel or reschedule once the visit is
  IN_DOCTOR_ROOM/LEFT (adapted from feat/lock-appointment-changes-after-
  visit-start, 8642082). Both rules are repeated in the repository WHERE so
  a concurrent transition cannot slip between check and write.
- PM-APPT-03: WAITING -> IN_DOCTOR_ROOM only on the slot's calendar day in
  the branch IANA zone; IN_DOCTOR_ROOM -> LEFT always, so a visit begun at
  23:30 can finish after midnight.
- PM-APPT-04: LEFT completes the appointment in the same write; the expiry
  sweep marks NO_SHOW only for still-CONFIRMED unattended visits (TIME_EXPIRED
  on finished rows stays reconciliation) and moves no money. The three sweep
  updates now share one transaction. Historical rows: reviewed, dry-run-by-
  default script in prisma/data-migrations/ (not auto-run by migrate deploy).
- PM-APPT-05: provider cancellation is DOCTOR-only (route + use-case);
  assistants keep reschedule and visit status within their assigned
  branches (existing clinic_staff_assignments scope).

Unit, disposable-DB integration and e2e tests cover the boundaries,
summer/winter and cross-midnight cases, assistant negatives, and the
attended/past-appointment refund holes reproduced on 2026-10-03.

