From 11cf8725a064777aa2e7e746b5666441490d9ffb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 05:15:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] fix(appointments): refuse patient bookings on a slot that
 has already started
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A patient could hold and confirm a slot whose start time had passed
(reproduced on a disposable DB: an hour-old slot became a CONFIRMED
booking), e.g. from a slot list loaded before the start. Under PM-APPT-01
such a booking could not be cancelled by the patient and would be swept to
NO_SHOW. Patient hold creation and the patient's reschedule target now
require now < start_at (422 SLOT_ALREADY_STARTED) — the same boundary as
PM-APPT-01, no lead time. Staff walk-ins and provider reschedules are
unchanged.

